---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const BASE_URL = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="AI Research Radar — Updates">
  <main class="project">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="crumb"><a href={BASE_URL + 'projects/research-radar'}>AI Research Radar</a></p>
      <h1>Updates</h1>
      <nav class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={BASE_URL + 'projects/research-radar/learnings'}>Learnings</a>
        <a class="btn" href={BASE_URL + 'projects/research-radar/design-decisions'}>Design decisions</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/alawal1/research-radar" target="_blank" rel="noopener">⌥ Code</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="crumb" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        <a href={BASE_URL + 'projects/research-radar'}>← Back to project</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h3>2026-10-02 — Deployed to GitHub Actions</h3>
      <p>
        Added a weekly cron so the agent runs on its own every Monday. Without this, the
        agent was a script I had to trigger manually — the whole point of a weekly digest
        is that it arrives without me pressing a button.
      </p>

      <h3>2026-10-02 — Digest delivery via committed markdown</h3>
      <p>
        Moved the digest from the Actions log to <code>data/digests/YYYY-MM-DD.md</code>,
        committed to the repo each week. I tried Google Docs delivery first, but service
        accounts can't create files in personal Drives, and OAuth for a personal Gmail is
        more work than the feature is worth. Markdown files are readable, permanent, and
        zero-auth.
      </p>

      <h3>2026-10-02 — Split CSV sync from the agent</h3>
      <p>
        Moved Google Sheets writes out of the agent and into a separate local script
        (<code>sync_to_sheet.py</code>). The cloud version kept hitting a 404 with
        credentials that worked locally. Rather than fight it, the agent always writes CSV,
        and the local machine syncs to Sheets on demand.
      </p>

      <h3>2026-10-01 — Tightened Gate 1</h3>
      <p>
        Rejected education and institutional AI governance papers after a test run showed
        them dominating the digest. The prompt now requires governance to be the primary
        contribution, not a secondary angle — and rejects academic-sector governance as a
        separate field from corporate and regulatory governance.
      </p>

      <h3>2026-10-01 — Added dedupe by title</h3>
      <p>
        Same papers were appearing twice with different OpenAlex IDs (once on arXiv, once
        on Zenodo). Added a normalization step: lowercase, strip punctuation, keep the
        first occurrence. The digest no longer repeats itself.
      </p>

      <h3>2026-09-30 — First working end-to-end run</h3>
      <p>
        The full pipeline worked for the first time: search → gates → extraction → digest
        → sheet. Fourteen papers found, ten kept, five written. The digest was readable but
        noisy — which set off the next week of tightening.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="back"><a href={BASE_URL + 'projects/research-radar'}>← Back to project</a></p>
  </main>

</Layout>
